{"step_index":96,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-22T09:05:37Z","content":"Use a `::after` pseudo-element on `.daily-options` — positioned to cover the right bleed edge with a gradient to bg color.","thinking":"The user wants to add a fade/opacity gradient on the right side of the daily options grid to indicate that there are more cards to scroll to. This is typically done with a pseudo-element (::after) on the wrapper element.\n\nThe grid itself has overflow-x: auto, so I need to put the gradient on the parent `.daily-options` wrapper using a `::after` pseudo-element with `pointer-events: none` so it doesn't block scrolling.\n\nHowever, the parent `.daily-options` needs `position: relative` for the pseudo-element to be positioned correctly, and the pseudo-element needs to be positioned absolutely on the right side.\n\nLet me add a `::after` pseudo-element to `.daily-options` that creates a gradient from transparent to the background color on the right side. I need to be careful about positioning since the grid has negative margins.\nSince the grid bleeds out 40px beyond the wrapper due to its negative margins and matching padding, I realize the pseudo-element should be positioned at `right: -40px` on `.daily-options` so it aligns with the actual visual edge of the scrolling content rather than the wrapper's own boundary.","tool_calls":[{"name":"replace_file_content","args":{"AllowMultiple":false,"Description":"Adds a right-fade gradient via ::after pseudo-element. Positioned to align with the grid's right bleed edge (-40px). pointer-events:none so it doesn't block scrolling or clicks.","EndLine":6,"Instruction":"Add position:relative to .daily-options and a ::after fade gradient on the right","ReplacementContent":".daily-options {\n  display: flex;\n  flex-direction: column;\n  gap: 16px;\n  width: 100%;\n  position: relative;\n}\n\n.daily-options::after {\n  content: \"\";\n  position: absolute;\n  top: 0;\n  right: -40px;\n  width: 80px;\n  height: 100%;\n  background: linear-gradient(to right, transparent, var(--color-bg));\n  pointer-events: none;\n  z-index: 1;\n}\n\n@media (max-width: 600px) {\n  .daily-options::after {\n    right: -16px;\n    width: 48px;\n  }\n}\n","StartLine":1,"TargetContent":".daily-options {\n  display: flex;\n  flex-direction: column;\n  gap: 16px;\n  width: 100%;\n}\n","TargetFile":"/home/gaitano/01-studio/01-src/moringa-marines/module-6/Mealy-Front---End-build-/src/components/DailyMealOptions/DailyMealOptions.css","toolAction":"Adding right fade gradient","toolSummary":"Add opacity gradient to grid"}}]}
